            <ArticleTitle>Ewing's sarcoma of the ilium presenting as unilateral sacroiliitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1109-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 24-year-old man who presented with unilateral sacroiliac pain associated with constitutional symptoms. Subsequent biopsy and pathohistologic evaluation demonstrated Ewing's sarcoma. We emphasize a consideration of Ewing's sarcoma in the differential diagnosis of unilateral sacroiliac pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
